//! Exact issuance and revocation vectors generated by the pinned TypeScript reference.
//!
//! As with Roadmap 6.1, the ported unit is a set of expressions rather than an exported function,
//! so the fixture proves provenance as well as output: `declarations` holds the `iss` and `rev`
//! constructions, the interaction that anchors either, and both attachment serializers, all read
//! out of the reference's own syntax tree by its own compiler. `pinned_artifacts` anchors the set
//! against values the reference's own test suite publishes — an `iss` SAID, an `ixn`, and two
//! attachment strings embedded inside its IPEX grant assertion — and `pinned_serializers` against
//! the two vectors `test/core/utils.test.ts` asserts directly.

